;; A local hint, and Wrongwater's way out: its one-row passage comes through
;; this room's west wall on row 4 (columns 0-8) and ends at a lip four rows
;; over the floor, so nothing here climbs back to it. Keep the row-3 roof
;; over columns 9-10. The passage is a quiet-exit, so the tells do not light
;; or sound it as a way out. One drop rises from the small pool (11-13) toward its
;; stain.
(room
  region: pipes
  at: (1 8)
  title: "Against the Drip"
  intent: "behind a thin stone curtain one drop rises toward its ceiling stain: a breath and a wrong thing"
  bed: (wind 0 water 0.7 pipes 0.2 drone 0.3)
  light: 0.33
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "#########################"
   "###########   ###########"
   "###########   ###########"
   "                      ###"
   "#########         |   ###"
   "#########         ||     "
   "########          ||     "
   "########          ||     "
   "###########~~~###########"
   "#########################")
  things: ((lantern-moth at: (20 5) count: 3 drawn: 3)
           (upward-drip at: (12 8))
           (mural at: (14 5) image: violet-well)
           (quiet-exit at: (0 4)))
  decor: auto)
